~ archivist_start
Archivist (calm, echoing): …So the armor returns.
Archivist: And this time, it walks without memory.
Archivist: Curious.

- Who are you? => archivist_intro
- Step back. I don’t want trouble. => archivist_intro
- …(silent) => archivist_intro


~ archivist_intro
Archivist (bowing slightly): I am the Archivist.
Archivist: Keeper of oaths. Keeper of names.
Archivist: Keeper of everything the Crescent erased.

Archivist: You are loud in the records… and yet empty.

- What do you mean “empty”? => archivist_memory
- You know who I was? => archivist_memory


~ archivist_memory
Archivist (sad): I know who you *were*.
Archivist: You volunteered.
Archivist: Not for power — but to carry guilt no one else could bear.

Archivist: The armor was never meant to obey.
Archivist: It was meant to *continue*.

- Continue what? => archivist_truth
- I didn’t agree to this. => archivist_truth


~ archivist_truth
Archivist: Order.
Archivist: When rulers fall.
Archivist: When knights hesitate.
Archivist: When mercy slows the blade.

Archivist: The Crescent does not rule the world.
Archivist: It prevents it from changing.

Archivist: And you were its sharpest edge.

- Then why can’t I remember any of this? => archivist_erasure
- So the monsters… the villages… => archivist_erasure


~ archivist_erasure
Archivist: Memory was the price.
Archivist: Those who remembered broke.
Archivist: Those who forgot endured.

Archivist (closer): You asked for this.
Archivist: You begged me to seal your past.

Archivist: And now the seal is failing.

- Failing how? => archivist_warning
- Tell me how to remove the armor. => archivist_warning


~ archivist_warning
Archivist (tense): You cannot.
Archivist: Not fully.

Archivist: The armor reacts to threats before you do.
Archivist: It chooses violence when you hesitate.

Archivist: And now—

[wait=0.4]
Archivist (alarmed): —it has identified *me* as a risk.

do GameState.player_attack_villager.emit()
do GameState.archivist_hurt.emit()

- I’m not attacking you! => archivist_loss
- Fight it— stop! => archivist_loss

~ archivist_loss
Archivist (urgent): You must listen—
Archivist: The Crescent’s heart lies beyond the Gate—
Archivist: The Captain is not its master—

do GameState.player_attack_villager.emit()
do GameState.archivist_hurt.emit()

Archivist (pained): …Ah.
Archivist: So it has decided.

- I didn’t mean to— => archivist_end
- Stay back! => archivist_end


~ archivist_end
Archivist (weak, fading glow): Do not lie to yourself.
Archivist: Intention no longer matters.

Archivist: When you face the Captain—
Archivist: You will not be choosing *what to do*…

Archivist: …only *what to become*.
do GameState.player_attack_villager.emit()
do GameState.archivist_hurt.emit()

[wait=0.1]
do GameState.archivist_death.emit()
=> END
